A td or th that isn’t in a table now gets no implicit role in Ladybird,
and Blink, WebKit and Gecko all do the same. Blink’s AXNodeObject::
DetermineTableCellRole() returns kGenericContainer without a
table-row and table ancestor. WebKit’s AccessibilityNodeObject::
isExposedTableCell() is false without an exposable parentTable(). And
Gecko’s td entry in HTMLMarkupMap.inc makes no table-cell accessible
unless its context is a table row.
